  "replay_controls": {
    "method": "Replay a captured menu frame with its original assets and vary the translated shaders. Read the visible-instance buffer after each compute pass, the four post-vertex positions, the material texture accesses and the 32 color-grading volume slices.",
    "instance_culling": "The original shaders read visible-instance index 131586 at slot 38984. The GPU scene buffer has 40960 entries, and all four projected positions were NaN. Translating the packed work items at their eight-byte stride made the original compute pass write instance 1984 to that slot. All four vertices then had finite positions, and the authored pixel shader sampled its curve atlas, fog and digital-rain flipbook.",
    "color_grading": "The translated pixel ancillary input supplies the render-target array layer to the color-grading shader. The original volume had one distinct slice repeated 32 times and 22 distinct colors. The corrected volume had 32 distinct slices and 23035 distinct colors.",
    "observation": "Both shader changes together displayed the authored green glyphs and the game UI in the replay. The columns are brighter before tone mapping than in the final menu."
  },
